From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] core: read a QML file past its header only for its blocks

The scanner read every line of every QML file at each start, building
the file's text again line by line, though past the header it looks
only for the preprocessor's blocks. A file with no "//@ if" now stops
at its header. Under callgrind, the scan was 12 percent of a shell's
start on its main thread, before anything loaded.

diff --git a/src/core/scan.cpp b/src/core/scan.cpp
index 9f33302..b908b92 100644
--- a/src/core/scan.cpp
+++ b/src/core/scan.cpp
@@ -151,7 +151,12 @@ bool QmlScanner::scanQmlFile(const QString& path, bool& singleton, bool& interna
 		this->scanErrors.append({.file = path, .message = std::move(error), .line = lineNum});
 	};
 
+	// Past its header, a file is read only for its preprocessor blocks, so one
+	// with none is read no further than its header.
+	const bool preprocessed = fileData.contains("//@ if");
+
 	while (!stream.atEnd()) {
+		if (!inHeader && !preprocessed) break;
 		++lineNum;
 		bool hideMask = false;
 		auto rawLine = stream.readLine();
